{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":503},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":26,"fleet_refs":27,"flight":31,"name":484,"type":485,"first":486,"description":487,"events":488,"vehicle_stage":33},"maven","NASA","National Aeronautics and Space Administration / Goddard Space Flight Center","gov","MARS","#0B3D91",2013,"FLOWN","2013-11-18","2014-09-22",308,"Atlas V 401","2454 kg","~3.5 km/s","good","© NASA / Goddard — public domain. Studied how Mars lost its atmosphere; served as relay for surface assets until contact was lost in December 2025.",[19,23],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"MAVEN — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MAVEN","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":22},"MAVEN mission (NASA)","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/maven/","measured",[28],{"id":29,"role":30},"atlas-v","launcher",{"launch":32,"cruise":37,"arrival":40,"totals":46,"events":49,"interplanetary_profile":93},{"vehicle_stage":33,"c3_km2_s2":34,"mass_at_tli_kg":35,"source":36},"Centaur upper stage (Atlas V 401)",12.2,2454,"NASA MAVEN Press Kit (2013-11)",{"tcm_count":38,"source":39},6,"NASA MAVEN Mission Operations Report",{"v_infinity_km_s":41,"periapsis_km":42,"inclination_deg":43,"orbit_insertion_dv_km_s":44,"source":45},2.59,150,75,1.22,"NASA MAVEN MOI Report (2014-09)",{"total_dv_km_s":47,"tli_or_tmi_dv_km_s":48,"source":36},3.5,2,[50,55,60,65,69,73,76,80,84,88],{"met_days":51,"type":52,"label":53,"description":54},0,"launch","Launch — Atlas V 401","Cape Canaveral, 2013-11-18. MAVEN (Mars Atmosphere and Volatile EvolutioN) was designed to characterise how Mars lost its atmosphere — measuring the present-day atmospheric-escape rates that scaled backward in time explain how the planet went from a wet, dense atmosphere ~3.8 Gyr ago to today's thin CO₂ shell.",{"met_days"